This project is an independent reimplementation of ideas from oh-my-pi (omp),
which is also MIT licensed:

    https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi
    Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner
    Copyright (c) 2025-2026 Can Bölük

    ...itself a fork of Pi by Mario Zechner:
    https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono
    Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner

No source code from either project is included here. All code in this
repository was written from scratch against a different runtime (Node, for
Claude Code hooks; omp is TypeScript and Rust). What is borrowed is design:
the lazy-rule / TTSR concept, the structural-outline read, and terminology
such as "matcherDigest". One format string -- the <system-interrupt> envelope
used in rule violation messages -- is reproduced verbatim from omp's TTSR
interrupt template. See the Credits section of README.md.

The MIT notices above are reproduced as attribution. Not affiliated with,
sponsored by, or endorsed by the oh-my-pi or Pi projects.

